# promise: crash-alerts-helper-bare-launch
# Someone clicks a Cra notification after its Alerts helper quit: macOS launches the helper app with no arguments.
# Chrome's helper sees that and exits quietly (chrome_main_mac.mm); Cra's notifications come from the Aperitif
# Alerts helper (AperitifHelpers), which Chrome's check missed, so it stopped on "Helper application requires
# --type" (a 0.1.46 crash report). cra-alerts-helper-launch.patch counts it as the Alerts helper too.
bare-helper Alerts
bare-helper Aperitif Alerts
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=after
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=after
